Scenario 3 — Cherry-Picked Commits

Identify cherry-picked commits.

Because cherry-picking changes commit IDs, do not rely only on commit ID equality.

Detect the relationship appropriately.

A valid cherry-picked commit should not incorrectly appear as a violation.

⸻

Scenario 4 — Direct Release Branch Commits

Identify commits that were committed directly to the release branch and are not present in the main branch.

Preserve the existing behavior.

⸻

Scenario 5 — Previous/Future Fix Version

If a commit contains:

* Previous Fix Version
* Future Fix Version
* Missing Fix Version
* Invalid Fix Version

the existing Java behavior must be retained.

